@juxt 3.4
# PHP2Shell fix: CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619 (critical, exploited in the wild)
# Run it: tell your AI agent "use juxt: run juxt/php2shell.juxt"
# No Juxt installed? Paste this whole file into any AI agent that can run commands.
# Sources: watchtowr.com/intelligence/php-cve-2026-109618-faq, cisa.gov alert 2026-10-21

objective: find every PHP that serves web traffic here and update it past PHP2Shell

context:
  fixed:        8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36, 8.2.35
  backport:     8.1, 8.0, 7.4 have no official release; use a distro or LTS vendor package, or upgrade
  unsupported:  7.3 and older; upgrade to a supported branch
  setups:       php-fpm, Apache mod_php (highest risk), php-cgi, LiteSpeed, FrankenPHP, Docker php images

constraints:
  MUST     check the PHP that serves web requests, not only the command-line php
  MUST     show what you found and the exact commands, then wait for my approval before changing anything
  MUST     update with the system package manager or a newer base image tag
  MUST     restart every PHP worker after the update
  MUST NOT present a configuration change as a fix; PHP says none mitigates this
  MUST NOT build PHP from source unless I ask
  SHOULD   start with internet-facing servers, Apache mod_php first
  OPEN     if it cannot be updated today, should I cut its internet access until it can?

verify:
  test "every web-serving PHP is at or above the fixed version for its branch"
  test "the version reported by the web server matches the installed package"
  review every PHP worker was restarted after the update

returns: report of versions before and after, what was restarted, anything still vulnerable
